---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy — Unknown Sender"
  description="How refunds, transfers and cancellations work for Unknown Sender bookings."
  canonicalPath="/refunds"
>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
      <div class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</div>

      <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>Unknown Sender tickets are valid for 90 days from the date of purchase and can be
          redeemed at any time within that window. If your plans change, you have flexibility,
          this page covers exactly how much and when.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Before you&rsquo;ve started the game</h2>
        <p>If you haven&rsquo;t redeemed the booking (i.e. you haven&rsquo;t begun a session), you can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Request a full refund within 14 days of purchase</strong> for any reason,
            in line with UK Consumer Contracts Regulations. Email us and we&rsquo;ll process it within
            5 working days.</li>
          <li><strong>Transfer your booking to another person</strong> at any time within the 90-day
            validity window. Email us with their name and email and we&rsquo;ll reassign it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>After you&rsquo;ve started the game</h2>
        <p>Once you press &ldquo;Start&rdquo; and the game begins delivering content, the ticket is
          considered used and is non-refundable. If you have a genuine reason you couldn&rsquo;t continue,
          a technical fault, an unsafe situation, weather that turned dangerous, email us and we&rsquo;ll
          look at it case by case.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>If we cancel or the experience is unavailable</h2>
        <p>If we take the game you&rsquo;ve booked offline temporarily (a location closes, a
          required venue is unavailable, etc.) before you&rsquo;ve started, we&rsquo;ll notify you and
          offer a full refund or an extension to your validity window, your choice.</p>
        <p>If a live session is interrupted by a technical failure on our side, we&rsquo;ll either restart
          the session at no extra cost or issue a full refund.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How to request</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@unknownsender.co.uk">hello@unknownsender.co.uk</a> with your
          booking code and a short explanation. We aim to respond within two working days.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Statutory rights</h2>
        <p>Nothing in this policy affects your statutory consumer rights under UK law.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding: 80px 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin: 12px 0 12px; }
  .updated { color: var(--ink-dim); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 40px; }

  section { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--ink-dim); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  p { margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
  a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
